    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The suite's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it's green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `customerCode` (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) is assigned once at owner creation and persisted, so `GET` returns the value fixed at that moment (a read-time computation would be wrong, since the global owner count keeps growing).\n\nChanges, kept as small cohesive units:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically from the entity (no mapper change needed).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` column field, a getter, and one new self-contained method:\n   ```java\n   public void assignCustomerCode(int ownerCount) {\n       String prefix = getLastName().substring(0, Math.min(3, getLastName().length())).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);\n       this.customerCode = String.format(\"%s-%04d\", prefix, ownerCount + 1);\n   }\n   ```\n   All the formatting logic lives here (CC 1), keeping the call site trivial.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 a 3-line guard that assigns the code only for new owners, using the live owner count:\n   ```java\n   if (owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {\n       owner.assignCustomerCode(ownerRepository.findAll().size());\n   }\n   ```\n   Because Hibernate auto-flushes before the `findAll` query, the second created owner sees the first, so `NNNN` increments by exactly one (`SMI-000N`, then `JON-000N+1`).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (test DB uses `ddl-auto=none`) and a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts so they still match the row shape. These are data-only edits with no code complexity. The default runtime profile (h2, `ddl-auto=update`) picks up the column automatically.\n\nI only touched the two Java methods strictly needed and pushed the actual logic into a new low-complexity method on `Owner`, avoiding growth in the large service/controller classes.",
